        <article class="section-card" id="research-2022">
          <span class="section-badge amber">RESEARCH (~2022) · KFDA MEDICAL EXOSKELETON (6 HOSPITALS) &amp; AI THERAPIST</span>
          <h2>Gait Rehabilitation Exoskeletons (SUBAR) &amp; Clinical AI Therapist</h2>
          <p>
            During my B.S. (2016), M.S. (2018), and Ph.D. (2022) in Mechanical Engineering at <strong>Sogang University</strong>, I engineered mechanical actuators, assist-as-needed adaptive impedance controllers, and clinical machine-learning software for lower-limb gait rehabilitation exoskeletons. Our team earned medical device certification from the <strong>Korea Food and Drug Administration (KFDA)</strong> and deployed the <strong>SUBAR</strong> exoskeleton across <strong>6 clinical hospitals</strong> in Korea. Across three years of hospital trials with stroke patients and physical therapists, I collected multi-sensor human-robot interaction telemetry to train and deploy the clinical <strong>AI Therapist</strong> (<em>IEEE TNSRE</em> 2019, 2020; <em>IEEE BioRob</em> 2020).
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Engineering Stack (2015–2022):</strong> Nonlinear and adaptive impedance control, machine learning (ANFIS, PSO, reinforcement learning), physical human-robot interaction (HRI), mechanical CAD (Siemens NX, SolidWorks), OpenSim musculoskeletal modeling, and real-time software in C/C++, Python, MATLAB/Simulink, LabVIEW, and ROS.
          </p>

